// A `comptime` parameter read as a VALUE inside a template that nothing instantiates. The
// uninstantiated-template probe binds the parameter to a placeholder marked `probe` (a probe has no
// argument of its own), so `N` reads as a number and nothing judges by it — it must never be reported as
// unresolved. Both halves of the probe are pinned: a generic function and a generic type (KR-137).
fn int32 scaled<T>(T x) comptime(int32 N) { return N + 1; }
type value Buf<T> comptime(int32 N) {
    T v;
    public ctor of(T v) { this.v = v; }
    public fn int32 cap() { return N; }
}
fn uint8 main() { return 0; }
